            <ArticleTitle>Coronary angiography--a curative procedure?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>428-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mehy.2012.01.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is increasing evidence, currently mainly subjective that, in addition to the diagnostic role; coronary angiography may have some degree of therapeutic effect, at least in some patients. Patients' experiences and known biological properties of the contrast media lend credence to this possibility and should be a spur for proper studies of the hypothesis.</AbstractText>
